    "note": "**TAKE 4 — double-click edits THE LINE UNDER THE POINTER** (founder on take 3: \"this isnt that great actually because its not aware of which text is here\").\n\n| Before | Now |\n|---|---|\n| A code run bound to `states[i]` = the WHOLE multi-line state; the inline editor put all of it in a token-sized single-line box | Every run binds **one line** of its state (`range`, raw-prop character span) and names **its own token** (`focus`). Double-click a token → the editor shows that line in a box aligned to the line (monospace, JetBrains Mono), the token pre-selected; Enter splices the edited line back into the state — the rest of the state is untouched. Removed (fading) lines edit the previous state's line |\n\nPlatform feature, not a template hack: `source.editor.binding.range` / `.focus` (@m0saic/types) · `bindingRange()` validation in @m0saic/platform (string leaves only; malformed ranges fall back to whole-leaf edits) · `bindPropRange()` in template-utils for authors (lyrics / captions / any multi-line string prop can use it) · Make: bindings index + edit hook (slice on open, splice on commit, span-aware re-anchor) + editor box (line-wide, token selected). Offsets index the RAW prop — tabs (`tabWidth`) and CRLF map back correctly.\n\nRecipe unchanged (pure defaults, 2 states, 7.5s, full bleed). Locks: 213 core (platform 5 new, template-utils 1, gate-32 range lock incl. tabs/CRLF/deletes) + 51 Make editor tests. Probe: default lite = 28 + 63 bound runs, 8 + 13 distinct lines, 0 focus/range mismatches.\n\nStill open: rise vs fade · cover/tutorial · CJK/emoji tofu · commit `code-png/`? · stress-01..10 (unchanged since take 3). Sizing of the multi-colour svg-text promotion (retires renderLite + sharp) is in chat.",
